## Problem

``POST /api/specialists``, ``PUT /api/specialists/:id`` and ``DELETE /api/specialists/:id`` forwarded the store's plain ``Error``s with no mapping, so four client mistakes came out as ``500 {"error":"Internal server error"}``:

- a taken name (``Specialist name already exists``);
- an unknown id on ``PUT`` or ``DELETE`` (``Specialist not found``);
- editing a built-in Specialist (its read-only message).

The settings pane prints the server's message verbatim, so the user got the generic text while the store already knew the reason. The neighbouring MCP-server surface answers ``400`` for its conflict and ``404`` for its missing id, so the Specialist routes were the outlier.

## Change

One guard around the three Specialist routes, keyed on the store's own rejection wording (the same shape ``services/api/src/http/custom-mcp.ts`` already uses):

- ``Specialist not found`` -> ``404``, message unchanged;
- every other rejection the store raises for these routes -> ``400``, message unchanged (required/limits, taken name, unavailable skills/connectors, built-in read-only, built-in delete, referenced-by-session, ``enabled`` type);
- everything else is a fault: the guard answers ``500 {"error":"Internal server error"}`` itself and logs ``unclassified_specialist_request_error`` with the method, the path and the message. It is deliberately not rethrown: the catch-all classifies an unknown error by its message, and a failed ``saveCatalog()`` surfaces ``node:sqlite``'s ``cannot start a transaction within a transaction`` (``code: "ERR_SQLITE_ERROR"``), which would answer ``400`` with the raw driver text. Only ``ApiStatusError``, ``SessionStoreHttpError`` and ``code === "SPECIALIST_RUNTIME_INVALID"`` — the three the catch-all maps without reading the message — still go through it.

No store message, no validation rule and no client code changed.

## Verification

- ``node --import tsx --test src/specialists-http.test.ts`` (from ``services/api``) — 16 tests, 16 pass, against a real ``createApiServer`` on a temp data dir:
  - duplicate name ``400`` with ``Specialist name already exists``; first create still ``201``;
  - unknown id ``404`` on ``PUT`` and on ``DELETE``;
  - built-in edit ``400`` with its read-only message; ``PUT {"enabled":false}`` still ``200`` and persists; built-in delete still ``400``;
  - six rejections driven through the real store keep their ``400`` and wording: missing name, 501-character description, 20 001-character instructions, unknown skill, unknown connector, ``{"enabled":"yes"}`` on a built-in — a wording change in ``store.ts`` fails these, not only a hand-copied list;
  - a coded ``node:sqlite`` fault (``code: "ERR_SQLITE_ERROR"``, "cannot start a transaction within a transaction") answers ``500 "Internal server error"``;
  - the guard's negatives: ``Catalog database is not initialized``, a ``TypeError``, ``ENOTDIR``, and messages that merely contain "must"/"cannot"/"invalid" stay faults.
- ``pnpm --filter @sciencediscovery/api typecheck`` — clean.
- ``pnpm ci:l1`` — 4/4 pass.

Fixes #935
